    <item>
      <title>Crafty Nutball - Jeff&amp;#039;s New Horizons Blog</title>
      <author>Jeff</author>
      <link>https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/2026/10/02/crafty-nutball/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/2026/10/02/crafty-nutball/</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 03:58:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;article id="post-9710" class="post-9710 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized"&gt; 	 	&lt;header class="entry-header"&gt; 		&lt;h1 class="entry-title"&gt;Crafty Nutball&lt;/h1&gt;	&lt;/header&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-header --&gt;  	&lt;div class="entry-content"&gt; 		 &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;On Monday, Kid Cat was trying to rip me off while selling me a kids&amp;#8217; smock. I turned down his first &lt;em&gt;three &lt;/em&gt;offers: He wanted 1,950 bells, then 1,500 bells, and then 1,050 bells for it. I thought he would give up after that, but he made a 4th offer too! It was under 1k (750 bells, to be exact), so I reluctantly bought it at that price. He called me a &amp;#8220;crafty nutball&amp;#8221; for outplaying him. Yeah, I don&amp;#8217;t think so. &lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img fetchpriority="high" width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/kidcat-nutball-sm.jpg" alt="Kid Cat: Take it away, you crafty nutball! Wow, I was totally outplayed." class="wp-image-9711" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Just be happy I bought it at all, Mr. Cat.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;When I started the game up on Tuesday, it was raining&amp;#8230;but also sunny. I figured I might see a rainbow at the top of the hour, and sure enough I did. A double rainbow, in fact.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/double-rainbow-sm.jpg" alt="A double rainbow in the sky over Forest." class="wp-image-9712" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Merengue also commented on it, telling me how happy she was to see it.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/merengue-double-sm.jpg" alt="Merengue: Hey, look at that! There's a double rainbow over us right now! I feel so happy after seeing that." class="wp-image-9713" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I still think rainbows are far too pale and colorless in this game, but it&amp;#8217;s nice to see it anyway.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;The next day, I spoke to Bob on the ramp going down to Sudden Valley and the camera shifted to an almost perfectly overhead view. It even made my fountain look like&amp;#8230; um, a valve.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/bob-overhead-sm.jpg" alt="Speaking with Bob from an overhead angle, looking straight down on a fountain." class="wp-image-9714" sizes="auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Here are a few other quick notes about the past week:&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;ul class="wp-block-list"&gt; &lt;li&gt;Last Sunday night, K.K. Slider performed &amp;#8220;K.K. Soul&amp;#8221; for me and Agent S.&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;On Tuesday, I gave some medicine to a sick Static. He rewarded me with a dragon suit.&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;Tonight, Bob asked me to deliver a gift (an explorer shirt) to Bones. Bones loved the gift, and he thanked me by giving me a sweatshirt.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; 	&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-content --&gt;  	 	&lt;footer class="entry-footer"&gt; 		&lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Posted on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/2026/10/02/crafty-nutball/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-10-02T23:58:00-04:00"&gt;October 2, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-10-03T01:32:11-04:00"&gt;October 3, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="byline"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Author &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="author vcard"&gt;&lt;a class="url fn n" href="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/author/jvgsjeff/"&gt;Jeff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;			&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-footer --&gt;  &lt;/article&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/kidcat-nutball-sm.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Fruits Giving - Jeff&amp;#039;s New Leaf Blog</title>
      <author>Jeff</author>
      <link>https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/2026/09/30/fruits-giving/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/2026/09/30/fruits-giving/</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 03:47:41 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;article id="post-18761" class="post-18761 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized"&gt; 	 	&lt;header class="entry-header"&gt; 		&lt;h1 class="entry-title"&gt;Fruits Giving&lt;/h1&gt;	&lt;/header&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-header --&gt;  	&lt;div class="entry-content"&gt; 		 &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;On Sunday, I found Boots in the &amp;#8220;green room&amp;#8221; at the aquarium. He threatened to eat me, after being inspired by fish. Probably the piranha. 😉&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img fetchpriority="high" width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20260927_HNI_0005.jpg" alt="Boots: I'll eat you!! I come here to get inspired by the fish... Don't you, at Nook's?" class="wp-image-18762" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Hornsby asked me to deliver an item to Lolly (an eight-ball tee that she left at his house), and she thanked me by giving me an orange. 🟠&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20260927_HNI_0009.jpg" alt="Lolly: It's an orange! It'll be a nice little snack for later!" class="wp-image-18763" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;When I returned to Hornsby, he was already asleep for the night. So I couldn&amp;#8217;t tell him the job was done! But I guess it doesn&amp;#8217;t matter much, since it&amp;#8217;s the recipient (Lolly, in this case) who gives the reward in this game.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;When I played tonight, I found M&amp;amp;M hanging out together. Molly was visiting Mira&amp;#8217;s house&amp;#8230;or is it her spaceship?&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20260930_HNI_0014.jpg" alt="Mira and Molly hang out in Mira's house." class="wp-image-18764" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;When I visited Boots, he was talking about his lullaboid. It looked like it was making him sleepy!&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20260930_HNI_0017.jpg" alt="Boots: That tone... It just draws you into a world of mystery, doesn't it?" class="wp-image-18765" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I found a lost item on the ground near the plaza, and it led me back to Boots&amp;#8217;s house. He said it was his bag, but it was missing some of the sand that was inside. He thinks someone must&amp;#8217;ve grabbed a handful of it and ran off. I&amp;#8217;m not sure why they couldn&amp;#8217;t just go down to the beach if they wanted some sand. Boots rewarded me with a pear. I guess my villagers are in a fruit-giving mood lately. 🍐&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20260930_HNI_0024.jpg" alt="Boots: Take my pear. A little thank-you from me to you." class="wp-image-18766" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Hornsby wanted to replace his evening cicada with something else, so I caught a cricket for him. He seemed to be happy with it, but it quickly met its fate!&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20260930_HNI_0027.jpg" alt="Hornsby: My new cricket will really liven up my place. A huh huh, I ate it!" class="wp-image-18767" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;figcaption class="wp-element-caption"&gt;Hornsby, NO!&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Nah, that was just his catchphrase. But he didn&amp;#8217;t reward me with fruit&amp;#8230;instead, he gave me the evening cicada that he was replacing. Oh joy.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/20260930_HNI_0028.jpg" alt="Hornsby: Well, I don't need my evening cicada anymore, so take it as my way of saying thanks!" class="wp-image-18768" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Do you know what I did with it? A huh huh, I ate it! 😋&lt;/p&gt; 	&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-content --&gt;  	 	&lt;footer class="entry-footer"&gt; 		&lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Posted on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/2026/09/30/fruits-giving/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-09-30T23:47:41-04:00"&gt;September 30, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-10-01T00:10:14-04:00"&gt;October 1, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="byline"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Author &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="author vcard"&gt;&lt;a class="url fn n" href="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/author/jvgsjeff/"&gt;Jeff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;			&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-footer --&gt;  &lt;/article&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20260927_HNI_0005.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Autumn Moon 2026 - Jeff&amp;#039;s ACCF Blog</title>
      <author>Jeff</author>
      <link>https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/2026/09/26/autumn-moon-2026/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/2026/09/26/autumn-moon-2026/</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 27 Sep 2026 03:55:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;article id="post-14183" class="post-14183 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized"&gt; 	 	&lt;header class="entry-header"&gt; 		&lt;h1 class="entry-title"&gt;Autumn Moon 2026&lt;/h1&gt;	&lt;/header&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-header --&gt;  	&lt;div class="entry-content"&gt; 		 &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;When I started up the game tonight, I was genuinely puzzled to see Mayor Tortimer standing outside of town hall. I knew it wasn&amp;#8217;t a holiday, and it wasn&amp;#8217;t Bug-Off day in this game (since it was held last week)&amp;#8230;and Tortimer doesn&amp;#8217;t host the Bug-Off in this game anyway. But he was there because the autumn moon (aka the harvest moon) was today.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img fetchpriority="high" width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/RUU_8651-sm.jpg" alt="Tortimer: Today is the Autumn Moon, sprout!" class="wp-image-14184" sizes="(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;He gave me a wheat bundle for the occasion. Thanks, Tortimer! Of course I later sold it at the shop&amp;#8230;but not for a dollar, because it wasn&amp;#8217;t &lt;em&gt;buck&lt;/em&gt;wheat.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I wanted to take a screenshot of the autumn moon, and I considered several locations around town. But I ultimately decided to snap the photo outside of the museum.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/RUU_8652-sm.jpg" alt="The autumn moon appears over the museum in Animal Crossing: City Folk (ACCF) for Wii." class="wp-image-14185" sizes="(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Inside the museum, I went down to the Roost. K.K. Slider was there for his usual Saturday night show. I asked him for a random song, and he performed &amp;#8220;Aloha K.K.&amp;#8221; for me. &lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/RUU_8653-sm.jpg" alt="K.K.: All right, get ready to dig the riffs on this ditty: Aloha K.K.." class="wp-image-14186" sizes="(max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;After the show, Cube asked me for a new catchphrase and I told him to say &amp;#8220;in a tray.&amp;#8221; I then listened in on a conversation between him and Bluebear. Bluebear asked Cube if he had any recommendations about where to go on vacation. Cube started off by saying he didn&amp;#8217;t used to like the snow much, but then he got sidetracked and talked about eating the snow. Bluebear got surprisingly angry that he went off on a tangent, even though it honestly wasn&amp;#8217;t bad at all.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/RUU_8654-sm.jpg" alt="Bluebear: GYA! I DIDN'T ASK ABOUT YOUR DUMB STORES! I ASKED YOU ABOUT...  Stop talking to me." class="wp-image-14187" sizes="auto, (max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Shortly after that, I went into Felicity&amp;#8217;s house. I was surprised to see that she was all packed up in boxes. She&amp;#8217;s moving out without warning, but I&amp;#8217;m not upset about it.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/RUU_8655-sm.jpg" alt="Felicity: Whoa, J-love! You showed up at the craziest time! I'm MOVING! Yeah, like, out of town!" class="wp-image-14188" sizes="auto, (max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;When I circled back around town, I spoke with Tortimer again. He said he loves the moon because it makes him feel round too.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="500" height="268" src="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/RUU_8656-sm.jpg" alt="Tortimer: I love the moon. Its roundness makes me feel all nice and round myself." class="wp-image-14189" sizes="auto, (max-width: 500px) 100vw, 500px" /&gt;&lt;figcaption class="wp-element-caption"&gt;We love the moon. &amp;#8216;Cause it is good to us&amp;#8230; 🎵&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Happy unexpected event day, everyone! 😆 See you next week!&lt;/p&gt; 	&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-content --&gt;  	 	&lt;footer class="entry-footer"&gt; 		&lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Posted on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/2026/09/26/autumn-moon-2026/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-09-26T23:55:00-04:00"&gt;September 26, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-09-27T02:25:16-04:00"&gt;September 27, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="byline"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Author &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="author vcard"&gt;&lt;a class="url fn n" href="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/author/jvgsjeff/"&gt;Jeff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;			&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-footer --&gt;  &lt;/article&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://www.jvgs.net/accfblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/RUU_8651-sm.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>One Last Bug-Off - Jeff&amp;#039;s New Horizons Blog</title>
      <author>Jeff</author>
      <link>https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/2026/09/26/one-last-bug-off/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/2026/09/26/one-last-bug-off/</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 27 Sep 2026 03:42:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;article id="post-9701" class="post-9701 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized"&gt; 	 	&lt;header class="entry-header"&gt; 		&lt;h1 class="entry-title"&gt;One Last Bug-Off&lt;/h1&gt;	&lt;/header&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-header --&gt;  	&lt;div class="entry-content"&gt; 		 &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;On Monday, my old friend Robin was camping at the campsite. (I&amp;#8217;ve recently had her in my City Folk and Wild World towns.) I did not invite her into this town, though.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img fetchpriority="high" width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/robin-camper-sm.jpg" alt="Robin, at the campsite: Oh, thank you for stopping by. I don't believe we've met. I'm Robin." class="wp-image-9702" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;The final Bug-Off of the year was held today, and I participated in one round. I caught nine bugs, scoring 11 points in the process.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/flick-11-sm.jpg" alt="Flick: Well done. You earned 11 points!" class="wp-image-9703" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;My score would&amp;#8217;ve (and should&amp;#8217;ve) been higher, but I saw a banded dragonfly and wasted too much time chasing it down. It disappeared before I could catch it. (They&amp;#8217;re too hard to resist, though.) But anyway, Flick paid me 3,075 bells for my nine bugs, and then I redeemed ten points for a bug cage.&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I do enjoy the villagers&amp;#8217; Bug-Off dialogue, though.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/savannah-netting-sm.jpg" alt="Savannah: Bug-Off days are so exciting! I'm not the best at netting bugs, but I'll still try to catch a bunch!" class="wp-image-9704" sizes="(max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;But they do look a bit silly in those hats. Well, especially when they wear the hat over a helmet.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/agents-catch-sm.jpg" alt="Agent S: Hi, lollipop. Mind if I watch you catch bugs for a little bit?" class="wp-image-9705" sizes="auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Later on, I noticed a former villager in town as a tourist. But it was someone who left very early on in Forest&amp;#8217;s history, Lopez. He&amp;#8217;s been gone so long that I almost forgot I had him. 😛 But it was nice to see him again regardless.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="700" height="394" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/lopez-tourist-sm.jpg" alt="Lopez: Yes! It's me, Lopez! I'm back on Forest, but this time as a basic tourist." class="wp-image-9706" sizes="auto, (max-width: 700px) 100vw, 700px" /&gt;&lt;figcaption class="wp-element-caption"&gt;You didn&amp;#8217;t have to call yourself basic.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Here are a few other quick notes about this week:&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;ul class="wp-block-list"&gt; &lt;li&gt;Last Sunday night, I recovered Wisp&amp;#8217;s spirits for him. He rewarded me with some tatami flooring.&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;I helped out Gulliver on Monday, and he sent me a samurai wig in the mail.&lt;/li&gt;    &lt;li&gt;Due to today&amp;#8217;s Bug-Off, K.K. Slider was not in town tonight.&lt;/li&gt; &lt;/ul&gt; 	&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-content --&gt;  	 	&lt;footer class="entry-footer"&gt; 		&lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Posted on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/2026/09/26/one-last-bug-off/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-09-26T23:42:00-04:00"&gt;September 26, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-09-27T01:51:05-04:00"&gt;September 27, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="byline"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Author &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="author vcard"&gt;&lt;a class="url fn n" href="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/author/jvgsjeff/"&gt;Jeff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;			&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-footer --&gt;  &lt;/article&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://www.jvgs.net/acnhblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/robin-camper-sm.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Maple&amp;#039;s Pic - Jeff&amp;#039;s ACWW Blog</title>
      <author>Jeff</author>
      <link>https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/2026/09/25/maples-pic/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/2026/09/25/maples-pic/</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 03:55:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;article id="post-9035" class="post-9035 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized"&gt; 	&lt;header class="entry-header"&gt; 		&lt;h1 class="entry-title"&gt;Maple&amp;#8217;s Pic&lt;/h1&gt;	&lt;/header&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-header --&gt;  	 	 	&lt;div class="entry-content"&gt; 		 &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Yesterday, Maple pinged me and told me I&amp;#8217;m the best friend she has in Forest. Aww. 😊 But the best part is that she then gave me her photo!!&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img fetchpriority="high" width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/maple-bff.jpg" alt="Maple: You're the best friend I've got here in Forest, so I want to give you this." class="wp-image-9036" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I took her picture home and put it on display, moving Truffles&amp;#8217;s pic to storage. 😛&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/maple-pic.jpg" alt="Maple's pic on display in my room of Gulliver items." class="wp-image-9037" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt; Maple&amp;#8217;s favorite quote is on the back: &amp;#8220;Maple + Moppina = BFF!&amp;#8221;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/maple-quote.jpg" alt="Quote on Maple's pic: Maple + Moppina = BFF!" class="wp-image-9038" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;figcaption class="wp-element-caption"&gt;I thought&lt;em&gt; I&lt;/em&gt; was your best friend.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Of course, Moppina is a reference to a villager conversation that I first saw in &lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/2018/10/30/moppina/"&gt;2018&lt;/a&gt;. Margie said that her mop&amp;#8217;s name is Moppina, and &amp;#8220;she&amp;#8221; is her best friend. (Other normal personality villagers can say the same thing.) It&amp;#8217;s an obscure reference to include on a villager&amp;#8217;s photo, but I appreciate details like that. 🙂&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I played again tonight, and it was raining in town. Chief told me that a while back, someone threw a wallet away near where we were standing.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/chief-wallet.jpg" alt="Chief: A while back, someone threw a wallet away around here." class="wp-image-9039" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;He said it was dirty and there was grease caked onto it, so that&amp;#8217;s why it was discarded.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/chief-grease.jpg" alt="Chief: It had dirty grease caked onto it, so that's why it got pitched, sparkles." class="wp-image-9040" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;But he said that was no excuse for wasting the wallet. I don&amp;#8217;t know, it probably smelled pretty bad if was caked in grease. They just shouldn&amp;#8217;t have discarded it on the ground. At least take it to the recycle bin!&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Pippy asked me to deliver a letter to Derwin, and she warned me not to read it. But Derwin clearly didn&amp;#8217;t feel the same way, because he gladly showed it to me. 😛&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="299" src="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/derwin-pippy-letter.jpg" alt="Hi, Derwin! Derwin! How's it shaking with you today? A glasses case is now mine! It rocks! -Pippy" class="wp-image-9041" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 85vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;When I returned to Pippy, she rewarded me with a stool.&lt;/p&gt; 	&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-content --&gt;  	&lt;footer class="entry-footer"&gt; 		&lt;span class="byline"&gt;&lt;img alt='' src='https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0ff365ea4b4ae589e18c26b092fe26946a6e14116b63065f41029c8c6138c7c8?s=98&amp;d=mm&amp;r=g' class='avatar avatar-49 photo' height='49' width='49'/&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Author &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="author vcard"&gt;&lt;a class="url fn n" href="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/author/jvgsjeff/"&gt;Jeff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Posted on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/2026/09/25/maples-pic/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-09-25T23:55:00-04:00"&gt;September 25, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-09-26T00:36:50-04:00"&gt;September 26, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;			&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-footer --&gt; &lt;/article&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://www.jvgs.net/acwwblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/maple-bff.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>House Swap? - Jeff&amp;#039;s New Leaf Blog</title>
      <author>Jeff</author>
      <link>https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/2026/09/21/house-swap/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/2026/09/21/house-swap/</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 02:58:15 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;article id="post-18749" class="post-18749 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized"&gt; 	 	&lt;header class="entry-header"&gt; 		&lt;h1 class="entry-title"&gt;House Swap?&lt;/h1&gt;	&lt;/header&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-header --&gt;  	&lt;div class="entry-content"&gt; 		 &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Last night, Mira asked me to bring her a piece of fresh fruit.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img fetchpriority="high" width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20260920_HNI_0081.jpg" alt="Mira: Awesome! You're the greatest! I'll be waiting! At Nook's!" class="wp-image-18750" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I gave her a perfect peach, and she rewarded me with an office desk. Outside of the context of Animal Crossing, the idea of trading a piece of fruit for an office desk sounds so ridiculous. 😆&lt;/p&gt;    &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Over at the campsite, Phoebe the &lt;s&gt;phoenix&lt;/s&gt; ostrich was camping. Her outfit was fire, and she seems pretty cool. But of course, my town is full.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20260920_HNI_0086.jpg" alt="Phoebe: I'm Phoebe! And you're... Jeff? Nice to meet you!" class="wp-image-18751" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;With some help from my monthly bank account interest, my savings balance has reached 140 million bells.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20260920_HNI_0089.jpg" alt="Your current balance is 140,000,000 bells." class="wp-image-18752" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I played again tonight, and Rolf wanted to play a game of hide-and-seek. He said it&amp;#8217;s an intellectual game where we try to read each other&amp;#8217;s minds. I&amp;#8217;m not quite sure that&amp;#8217;s an accurate description, but sure, I&amp;#8217;ll play!&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20260921_HNI_0091.jpg" alt="Rolf: It's a very intellectual game where the it and those hiding try to read each other's minds!" class="wp-image-18753" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;He gave me ten minutes to find him, Jeremiah, and Hornsby. Within two minutes, I had found two of them, but the interesting part is where they hid. Jeremiah was hiding behind Rolf&amp;#8217;s house&amp;#8230;&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20260921_HNI_0093.jpg" alt="Jeremiah: No! How'd you find me?! I was in super-stealth mode and everything!" class="wp-image-18754" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;And then Rolf returned the favor, hiding behind Jeremiah&amp;#8217;s house! It&amp;#8217;s like they swapped houses for the game! 😆&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20260921_HNI_0094.jpg" alt="Rolf tries to hide behind Jeremiah's house." class="wp-image-18755" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;I later found Hornsby behind a tree near the Roost to secure my victory.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20260921_HNI_0096.jpg" alt="Rolf: So it looks like the winner of this game is muscles!" class="wp-image-18756" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;Rolf gave me my prize: A new TV with VCR. What, was a rotary phone not available? 😆&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20260921_HNI_0097.jpg" alt="Rolf: Here. My TV with VCR is your reward! A good reward is the best way to remember victory!" class="wp-image-18757" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;figcaption class="wp-element-caption"&gt;In that case, I&amp;#8217;ve already forgotten it.&lt;/figcaption&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;   &lt;p class="wp-block-paragraph"&gt;When I walked up to the city, several of my former villagers were hanging out near the entrance. That included Daisy, Bob, Julian, and Lily. 😊&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div class="wp-block-image"&gt; &lt;figure class="aligncenter size-full"&gt;&lt;img width="400" height="240" src="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20260921_HNI_0004.jpg" alt="Daisy: I love how alive this part of town is!" class="wp-image-18758" sizes="auto, (max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" /&gt;&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;/div&gt;	&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-content --&gt;  	 	&lt;footer class="entry-footer"&gt; 		&lt;span class="posted-on"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Posted on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/2026/09/21/house-swap/" rel="bookmark"&gt;&lt;time class="entry-date published" datetime="2026-09-21T22:58:15-04:00"&gt;September 21, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;time class="updated" datetime="2026-09-21T22:58:16-04:00"&gt;September 21, 2026&lt;/time&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="byline"&gt;&lt;span class="screen-reader-text"&gt;Author &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="author vcard"&gt;&lt;a class="url fn n" href="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/author/jvgsjeff/"&gt;Jeff&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;			&lt;/footer&gt;&lt;!-- .entry-footer --&gt;  &lt;/article&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://www.jvgs.net/newleafblog/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/20260920_HNI_0081.jpg" type="image/jpeg"/>
    </item>
